#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:5
msgid "Protocol description"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:7
msgid "This protocol is considered a versioned public API. Once included in the `main` branch, it will not be changed without updating the IDENTIFY command response, other than as necessary to fix specification bugs or to refine Uɴᴘʀᴇᴅɪᴄᴛᴀʙʟᴇ behavior."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:10
msgid "Glossary"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:12
msgid "**Uɴᴘʀᴇᴅɪᴄᴛᴀʙʟᴇ**: Describes behavior that is not constrained by this specification. Frontends must avoid invoking such behavior."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:13
msgid "**Word**: 32-bit integer. Corresponds to the data path width and minimal addressable unit. Depending on data format, may contain multiple samples."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:14
msgid "**Block**: Multiple *words* containing sample data, terminated with a *trailer*. Samples are both internally processed and externally transmitted in blocks; during internal processing, blocks without an exceptional trailer may be merged to improve efficiency."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:15
msgid "**COBS**: [Consistent Overhead Byte Stuffing](https://www.stuartcheshire.org/papers/COBSforToN.pdf), a self-synchronizing transformation of byte streams used for efficiently inserting frame boundaries in streams of arbitrary binary data."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:16
msgid "**Trailer**: A single byte, placed last within a *COBS* frame containing a *block* of sample data. Indicates the exceptional nature of the last *word* within that block (whether it contains a trigger, overflow, or completion event). Zero if the last word is not exceptional."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:17
msgid "**Prolog**: Sample data returned before and immediately encompassing the trigger event. The last word of the prolog contains the sample that matched the trigger condition, or the sample that was being processed when a trigger was forced, which is indicated with the *trailer* of the last *block* of the prolog."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:18
msgid "**Epilog**: Sample data returned immediately after the *prolog*, and shortly after the trigger event. Can continue indefinitely if the transport conditions (bandwidth and latency) are sufficient."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:19
msgid "**FourCC**: [four-character code](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/FourCC), a sequence of four (wholly or in part printable-ASCII) bytes used as an identifier for data interchange."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:22
msgid "Overall framing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:24
msgid "The protocol relies on an underlying reliable bidirectional byte stream transport, such as TCP or USB. (In the latter case, packet boundaries are don't care for this protocol.) It places no specific requirements on the transport nor has mandatory out-of-band components. When using TCP as the underlying transport, port 5555 may be used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:26
msgid "The protocol has a command-response structure, with the host sending commands. The host-to-device direction has no framing; the device-to-host direction uses COBS to distinguish between command responses and sample data."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:29
msgid "It is expected that a streaming COBS decoder such as [ccobs](https://github.com/Elizafox/ccobs) is used to process the device-to-host data; the protocol places no limit on the maximum size of a COBS frame."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:32
msgid "The overall format of the device-to-host COBS frames is:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:38
msgid "The `index` denotes a *substream index*. Substream 0 contains command responses, substream 1 contains sample data."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:40
msgid "Responses to commands take priority over sample data; when a response is required by the protocol and sample data is currently being streamed, the current block of sample data will be interrupted, the response will be sent, and the streaming of sample data will resume. Such interruption is transparent to the protocol, and no special handling is required: the interrupted block becomes a well-formed block with a *normal* trailer marker."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:43
msgid "Command sequences"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:50
msgid "`type[7]`: whether there is a return value"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:51
msgid "`type[6]`: whether there is an argument"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:52
msgid "`type[5]`: whether the command is a common or a trigger command"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:53
msgid "`type[4..0]`: command code"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:56
msgid "Sample data sequences"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:62
msgid "`trailer[7..6]`: end marker of the data block:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:63
msgid "`00`: *normal*, expect more samples in next block"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:64
msgid "`11`: *complete*, there will be no more samples until another trigger occurs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:65
msgid "`10`: *trigger*, sub-word position described in bits 4..0"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:66
msgid "`01`: *overflow*, there are skipped samples *near* the last word"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:67
msgid "`trailer[4..0]`: how far off into the last word is the trigger position, in bits (e.g. 16 for \"second 14-bit sample\"); integer multiple of data stride"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:69
msgid "Because the overflow condition is not discovered until a sample is forced into the full queue, it is difficult to precisely pinpoint the exact location of this condition. The second-to-last word of a data block marked with the overflow trailer still contains good samples; the samples contained within the last word have Uɴᴘʀᴇᴅɪᴄᴛᴀʙʟᴇ values."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:72
msgid "Metadata request sequences"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:81
msgid "Common commands"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:83
msgid "These commands are a part of the base protocol and are independent of the selected trigger unit. They have types matching the mask `0bXX_0XXXXX`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:86
msgid "`0b10_000000`: IDENTIFY"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:88
msgid "`ret`: FourCC `0x30414c47`/`GLA0`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:90
msgid "Identifies the protocol version and confirms the ability to communicate with the device."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:93
msgid "This command **must** be the first one sent by the frontend. Any future revision of the protocol will preserve the exact framing of (at least) this specific command and is guaranteed to respond to it with the framing described in this document and a FourCC distinct from `GLA0`. Any other host-to-device byte sequence causes Uɴᴘʀᴇᴅɪᴄᴛᴀʙʟᴇ effects in this case."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:96
#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:105
#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:135
#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:167
msgid "The response to this command is fixed for any given logic analyzer instance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:99
msgid "`0b10_000001`: GET_CLK_FREQUENCY"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:101
msgid "`ret` (`clk_frequency`): reference frequency in Hz (e.g. 48'000'000 for 48 MHz)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:103
msgid "Returns the frequency of the reference clock of the sampling head. This value is used to convert a desired sample rate into a divisor value suitable for the SET_CLK_DIVISOR command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:108
msgid "`0b01_000010`: SET_CLK_DIVISOR"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:110
msgid "`arg[N..0]` (`clk_divisor`): clock divisor - 1 (e.g. 3 for DIV/4)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:112
msgid "Configures the reload value for the clock divisor contained in the sampling head. This command invalidates buffered sample data similarly to the INTERRUPT command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:114
msgid "If the value of `clk_divisor` is too high or too low, it is clamped to the lowest or highest valid value for this logic analyzer instance. In conjunction with the GET_CLK_DIVISOR command, this behavior can be used to probe the available range of divisor values."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:116
msgid "On startup, `clk_divisor` is Uɴᴘʀᴇᴅɪᴄᴛᴀʙʟᴇ."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:119
msgid "`0b10_000010`: GET_CLK_DIVISOR"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:121
msgid "`arg[N..0]` (`clk_divisor`): clock divisor - 1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:123
msgid "Returns the configured clock divisor reload value. Since the exact width (`N`) of the divisor register is unspecified, this command should be used to confirm that the desired clock divisor value is feasible."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:126
msgid "`0b10_000011`: GET_BUFFER_SIZE"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:128
msgid "`ret[29..0]` (`buffer_size`): capture buffer size in units of words (e.g. 0x40000 for 1 MB)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:130
msgid "Returns the maximum amount of data that can be stored within the device's onboard RAM. *This is not a limit on sampling length.* Instead, this value can be used to make some important inferences:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:132
msgid "If the sum of the prolog and epilog sizes is less than or equal to the capture buffer size, then the capture is guaranteed to complete unless it exceeds the RAM write bandwidth. If it is greater than the capture buffer size, then an overflow may be caused by unfavorable USB bandwidth or latency."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:133
msgid "The prolog size must be strictly less than the capture buffer size; if configured otherwise, the effect is Uɴᴘʀᴇᴅɪᴄᴛᴀʙʟᴇ. (There are no restrictions on the epilog size.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:138
msgid "`0b01_000100`: SET_PROLOG_SIZE"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:140
msgid "`arg[29..0]` (`prolog_size`): prolog size in units of words"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:142
msgid "Configures the upper bound on the amount of pre-trigger capture data that will be sent. Less data than `prolog_size` specifies may be sent if the trigger occurred too soon after a pipeline flush and the requested amount of data has not been sampled yet."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:144
msgid "At least one word of prolog must be transmitted, otherwise the data and offset of the *trigger* event cannot be communicated. If `prolog_size` is 0, the command acts as if `prolog_size` was set to 1."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:146
msgid "On startup, `prolog_size` is 1."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:149
msgid "`0b01_000101`: SET_EPILOG_SIZE"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:151
msgid "`arg[0..29]` (`epilog_size`): epilog size in units of words"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:152
msgid "`arg[31]` (`streaming`): whether to capture continuously instead"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:154
msgid "Configures the exact amount of post-trigger capture data that will be sent. If `streaming` is 1, then `epilog_size` is disregarded and samples are streamed continuously until an overflow occurs or an INTERRUPT command is received."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:156
msgid "At least one word of epilog must be transmitted, otherwise the *complete* event cannot be communicated. If `streaming` is 0 and `epilog_size` is 0, the command acts as `epilog_size` it was set to 1."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:158
msgid "On startup, `streaming` is 1."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:161
msgid "`0b10_000110`: GET_DATA_FORMAT"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:163
msgid "`ret` (`data_format`): FourCC describing sample data format"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:165
msgid "Describes the meaning of the sample data words."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:169
msgid "Unrecognized data formats must be reported by the frontend as an error unless there is an option to save the raw capture data for analysis with a different tool."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:172
msgid "Digital samples: FourCC `0x4944xxxx`/`DIxx`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:174
msgid "`data_format[0..4]` (`width`): how many bits are valid for each sample"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:175
msgid "`data_format[8..12]` (`stride`): how many bits to advance to get to the next sample (power-of-2, 1 to 32 inclusive)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:177
msgid "Describes the placement of digital samples within each word. Each sample starts on a power-of-2 bit index (a multiple of `stride`) and continuously occupies `width` bits. Therefore, a single word may contain 1, 2, 4, 8, 16, or 32 digital samples depending on the `width`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:179
msgid "First captured sample is placed in the least significant bits of the data word."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:182
msgid "Mixed analog/digital samples: FourCC `0x4e41xxxx`/`ANxx`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:184
msgid "This is a planned data format that hasn't been prototyped yet."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:187
msgid "`0b01_010000`: SET_TRIGGER"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:189
msgid "`arg` (`trigger`): FourCC of requested trigger block"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:191
msgid "When `arg` designates a valid trigger block, selects (enables) and resets this trigger block. Any other trigger blocks are disabled, and all commands matching the `0bXX_1XXXXX` mask are routed to the selected trigger block. When `arg` does not designate a valid trigger block, does nothing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:193
msgid "On startup, `trigger` is Uɴᴘʀᴇᴅɪᴄᴛᴀʙʟᴇ."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:195
msgid "Unrecognized trigger blocks must be reported by the frontend as an error unless there is an option to enter a custo configuration of trigger registers as a raw sequence of 32-bit trigger commands."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:197
msgid "Commands whose types match the mask `0bXX_1XXXXX` belong to the selected trigger unit. Many more types of triggers can exist than can be anticipated by the authors of this specification; this extension point allows the end user to customize the trigger conditions for any particular domain."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:200
msgid "`0b10_010000`: GET_TRIGGER"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:202
msgid "`ret` (`trigger`): FourCC of the selected trigger block"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:204
msgid "Identifies the currently selected trigger block. Can be used to confirm success of the SET_TRIGGER command, or to avoid resetting a trigger block that is already selected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:207
msgid "`0b10_010001`: GET_METADATA"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:209
msgid "`ret` (`metadata_format`): FourCC of the metadata format"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:211
msgid "Sends metadata as an uninterrupted frame in substream 2 after the normal command response."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:214
msgid "No metadata: FourCC `0x00000000`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:216
msgid "No metadata available. As a special case, there will be no substream 2 frame after this response."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:219
msgid "Channel name list: FourCC `NAME`/`0x454d414e`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:221
msgid "List of UTF-8 encoded channel names separated by NUL bytes. For example, the following hex dump corresponds to metadata for a 4-channel logic analyzer with channels named `CS#`, `CLK`, `COPI`, `CIPO`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:230
msgid "`0b11_011111`: SYNCHRONIZE"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:232
msgid "`arg`: any value"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:233
msgid "`ret`: `arg`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:235
msgid "Bounces the argument back. Can be used to re-establish command/response synchronization after an exceptional condition such as buffer overflow somewhere between the host and the device (not to be confused with an overflow condition during sampling)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:237
msgid "To avoid ambiguity, the argument should be a high-entropy value; at least, two consecutive invocations should not have the same argument."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:240
msgid "`0b00_000000`: ARM_TRIGGER"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:242
msgid "Enables the trigger unit. Once the trigger condition is fulfilled, the trigger unit is disabled, and sample data is returned as configured by `prolog_size`, `epilog_size`, and `streaming`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:245
msgid "`0b00_000001`: FORCE_TRIGGER"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:247
msgid "Forces a trigger condition to occur. Immediately after receiving this command, the trigger unit is disabled, and sample data is returned as with the ARM_TRIGGER command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:250
msgid "`0b00_000010`: DISARM_TRIGGER"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:252
msgid "Disables the trigger unit."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:255
msgid "`0b00_000011`: INTERRUPT"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:257
msgid "Stops any capture in progress, disables the trigger unit, and discards any accumulated capture data that would otherwise be returned as a part of the prolog of the following trigger event."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:260
msgid "Basic trigger: FourCC `0x49534142`/`BASI`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:262
msgid "Basic trigger module. Generates a trigger match if any of the per-bit conditions are satisfied. The possible per-bit conditions are: rising edge, falling edge, high level, low level."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:264
msgid "It is possible to modify the trigger condition after issuing the ARM_TRIGGER command. The updated condition takes effect immediately."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:267
msgid "`0b01_100000`: TRIG_BASIC_SET_ACTIVE"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:269
msgid "`arg[n]`: whether to match on channel `n`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:272
msgid "`0b01_100001`: TRIG_BASIC_SET_LEVEL"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:274
msgid "`arg[n]`: whether channel `n` is compared by level (1) or by edge (0)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:277
msgid "`0b01_100010`: TRIG_BASIC_SET_VALUE"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:279
msgid "`arg[n]` (if channel `n` is compared by edge): whether to match channel `n` on negative (0) or positive (1) edge"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:280
msgid "`arg[n]` (if channel `n` is compared by level): whether to match channel `n` on low (0) or high (1) level"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:283
msgid "`0b01_100011`: TRIG_BASIC_SET_ANYEDGE"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:285
msgid "`arg[n]` (if channel `n` is compared by edge): whether to match channel `n` on both positive and negative edges (1) or the edge specified by TRIG_BASIC_SET_VALUE (0)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../software/glasgow/applet/interface/analyzer2/protocol.md:286
msgid "`arg[n]` (if channel `n` is compared by level): Uɴᴘʀᴇᴅɪᴄᴛᴀʙʟᴇ behavior"
msgstr ""

